From 96504b5b412f37f14f5af3917ccfcb91a69b11a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aelin <aelin@postmarketos.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:11:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 004/107] Revert "CI: switch temporarily to non-alpine
 registry"

This reverts commit e1d0e1786f9f81b444ef684b9c13d4eac0c85fb3.

As I have mentioned previously in commit
47f342bfcbc44d97f123f23cfcc67b9651d2ce3e when we initially switched to
Alpine's registry and in commit 4e97050cf43f11a1581346602ca0f519b7c5da0e
the last time this incident of switching to Docker Hub happened, we
*cannot* use Docker Hub for our CI. It does not support loongarch64 for
official images at the moment. The only place where we can pull Alpine
images for loongarch64 from is Alpine's registry. The runners are
configured to pull the GitLab runner helper images from there as well,
because by default, the runner will attempt to pull them from Docker
Hub, where they don't exist.

Please stop going back and forth on this. Contrary to what Ollie says in
his comment at
https://gitlab.nura.eco/nura/pmaports/-/merge_requests/9841#note_593290,
changing the runner configuration for the loongarch64 machines will not
help. And I beg you to check the commit history before making me submit
this change for a fourth time in the future.

Note from Ollie: sorry for that. I did this because Alpine's registry
was briefly down: https://alpinelinux.org/posts/GitLab-security-incident-CVE-2026-97229.html
I forgot that the reason we do this is that other registries don't build
for loongarch64, so I've added a note for this now.

Part-of: <https://gitlab.nura.eco/nura/pmaports/-/merge_requests/9854>
---
 .ci/build-jobs.yaml.j2 | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.ci/build-jobs.yaml.j2 b/.ci/build-jobs.yaml.j2
index 05d03d1412..64e3b36d49 100644
--- a/.ci/build-jobs.yaml.j2
+++ b/.ci/build-jobs.yaml.j2
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
-image: alpine:3.24
+# Other registries don't have loongarch64 images!
+image: registry.alpinelinux.org/img/alpine:3.24
 stages:
   - build
   - hardware tests
-- 
2.53.0

